    "Type": 1,
    "Title": "Show HN: I made a Clojure-like language in Go, boots in 7ms",
    "Url": "https://github.com/nooga/let-go",
    "Description": "Let-go is a Clojure-like language (~90% compatible with JVM Clojure) written in pure Go. It ships as a ~10MB static binary and cold boots in ~7ms - that\u0026#x27;s about 50x faster than JVM and 3x faster than Babashka. It has decent throughput on algorithmic workloads - within ballpark of the GraalVM-backed sci.\u003Cp\u003EI started this project in 2021 as an elaborate practical joke: I wanted to have an excuse for writing Clojure while pretending to write Go.\u003Cp\u003EJokes aside, it turned out to be pretty decent",
